writingIdeas:[{viewpoint:'Education can improve social mobility.',topicSentence:'Accessible education can enable people from disadvantaged backgrounds to improve their long-term prospects.',collocations:['play a crucial role in','have access to','improve career prospects','break the cycle of poverty'],argument:'When high-quality schools and training are affordable, learners can gain qualifications that employers recognise. This improves access to stable work and may allow families to break the cycle of poverty over time.'},{viewpoint:'Schools should teach practical life skills.',topicSentence:'A balanced curriculum should prepare students for everyday responsibilities as well as examinations.',collocations:['manage personal finances','make informed decisions','enter the workforce','a well-rounded education'],argument:'Many school-leavers can pass academic tests but struggle with budgeting, communication or basic workplace expectations. Teaching these skills would make the transition to adult life smoother without replacing core academic subjects.'}],
